//==
// # Provenance, checks, diagnostics, reports
//
// Layer 0 of the STEP B-rep to mesh design. Provenance is the map from a
// result back to its source; a Check is a law evaluated over one value; a
// Diagnostic is a finding with a severity; a Report collects both. The chain
// is SPEC-DSL.md section 4: Law_X, then Check, then Diagnostic, then Report,
// then IsClean.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Provenance
//  - Severity
//  - Checks, diagnostics, reports

//==
// # Provenance

// Where a mesh vertex sits on the exact model: on the lowest-dimensional model
// cell that contains it (its carrier), with its parameter on that cell. A
// vertex at a model vertex, at parameter Parameter of an edge's curve, or at
// natural parameters Uv of a face's surface (radians or model lengths, not the
// stdlib's normalized UV). Re-evaluating the carrier at the parameter gives the
// vertex position within the length tolerance (layer 7).
type MeshVertexProvenance
    = OnVertex(Vertex: BrepVertexIndex)
    | OnEdge(Edge: BrepEdgeIndex, Parameter: Number)
    | OnFace(Face: BrepFaceIndex, Uv: UvCoordinate);

// What a check or diagnostic is about: nothing yet (Nowhere, a placeholder
// that Located replaces), the input as a whole (a text that is not Part 21,
// options that cannot be honoured, a model with no faces), a STEP instance, a
// curve or surface of the geometry arena (a defect in the geometry record
// itself, reported once and not at every edge or face that cites it), a
// topology object, or a mesh vertex or element. Every finding carries one so
// a user can go from the finding to the entity in the file.
type Provenance
    = Nowhere
    | WholeInput
    | AtInstance(Id: StepInstanceId)
    | KernelCurve(Index: CurveIndex)
    | KernelSurface(Index: SurfaceIndex)
    | KernelVertex(Index: BrepVertexIndex)
    | KernelEdge(Index: BrepEdgeIndex)
    | KernelLoop(Index: BrepLoopIndex)
    | KernelFace(Index: BrepFaceIndex)
    | KernelShell(Index: ShellIndex)
    | KernelBody(Index: BodyIndex)
    | MeshVertex(Index: VertexIndex)
    | MeshElement(Index: ElementIndex);

//==
// # Severity

// How bad a finding is. Error: the result cannot be trusted (IsClean fails).
// Warning: a geometric criterion exceeded by less than a factor of ten.
// Info: a quality threshold missed, or a remark.
type Severity
    = Error
    | Warning
    | Info;

// The three groups of constraint in the design's front README, which decide a
// failed check's severity (SeverityOf). Topological: exact statements about
// counts, indices, incidence, and orientation, structural rules of the file
// included. Geometric: a measured distance or angle against a tolerance or
// criterion. Quality: a preference with a threshold (minimum angle, aspect
// ratio). Always written qualified: ConstraintGroup.Geometric, since layer 7's
// ConformanceLevel also has a case Geometric.
type ConstraintGroup
    = Topological
    | Geometric
    | Quality;

//==
// # Checks, diagnostics, reports

// One law evaluated over one value, sampled where the law is pointwise. Law is
// the Law_ function's name; Worst is the worst measure seen, in the law's own
// unit and oriented so that larger is worse; Bound is the bound that sample
// was checked against (0 for an exact law), so per-point bounds survive the
// fold; Where is the provenance of the worst sample. Built only by
// CheckWithin, CheckExact, and WorseOf, so that Holds is exactly "Worst <=
// Bound" (Law_HoldsExactlyWhenWithinBound). Worst is NaN (Number.Unmeasured)
// when the measure could not be computed, and such a check fails
// (Law_UnmeasuredCheckFails).
type Check
{
    Law: String;
    Holds: Boolean;
    Worst: Number;
    Bound: Number;
    Where: Provenance;
}

// A finding: a failed check with its severity, or a problem found outside any
// check (an unsupported STEP entity). Code is the failed law's name, or a
// code of the producing layer for a finding outside any law; Message is a
// fixed sentence (Plato strings cannot be composed); Measure is the check's
// Worst, or NaN when the finding has no measure.
type Diagnostic
{
    Severity: Severity;
    Code: String;
    Message: String;
    Where: Provenance;
    Measure: Number;
}

// The checks and diagnostics of one validation. Built only by Empty, Merge,
// ReportOf, and Located, so that every failed check has a diagnostic
// (Law_FailedCheckHasDiagnostic). Reports form a monoid under Merge with
// Empty as identity.
type Report
{
    Checks: Array<Check>;
    Diagnostics: Array<Diagnostic>;
}
